      "id": "2125241517669228911",
      "text": "Over the last 30+ years I’ve aggressively bought every major dip on gold and silver. \n\nI always feel compelled to load up because all major governments run unsustainable deficits while their national debts balloon. \n\n‘Close enough’ to a bottom is ‘good enough’ for me as I know slight timing errors in the short run will be irrelevant in the long run.  \n\nIf they keep rates up, the economy collapses, tax revenue drops, deficits explode and they would have to issue mountains of debt with high interest rates and would enter a debt spiral where more and more printing of money is required.  \n\nIf they cut rates and drop interest rates to revive the economy then inflation will keep outpacing nominal yields. \n\nThere’s only one option to get levels back to a reasonable level and then keep and interest rate policy that provides an inflation adjusted return and while keeping inflation under control. \n\nThat choice is monetization of the debt. Where governments instruct their central banks to buy up the outstanding debt and then cancel the debt that has been purchased by their central bank.\n\nGold and silver will do very well anyway you slice it.  Just a matter of time.",
